   "source": [
    "### Convert the date column to datetime\n",
    "**Purpose:** `pd.to_datetime()` makes dates usable for time differences, chronological splitting and window generation. Without this conversion, `.diff()` between text strings produces an error. **Important:** chronological windows also require rows to be sorted by date; the displayed results below indicate daily ordering in this file, but explicit sorting is a useful safeguard in reusable code."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "metadata": {
    "id": "2gW5IaXwBolF"
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "sw90[\"date\"] = pd.to_datetime(sw90[\"date\"])\n",
    "sw17[\"date\"] = pd.to_datetime(sw17[\"date\"])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "ehMjExoOYmiO"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Verify consecutive daily observations\n",
    "**Purpose:** Compare each date with the previous date. The saved output shows **1,825 intervals of exactly one day** at both SW90 and SW17, meaning that—within their current ordering—there are no missing calendar days. This is essential: a three-row chunk should represent three consecutive **days**, not merely three arbitrary rows."
   ]
  },
