    "## 2. Build sliding-window chunks — SW90 only\n",
    "### Convert three days of measurements into one modeling row\n",
    "**Purpose:** For each consecutive three-day window, extract SW90 rainfall, soil moisture and river discharge for **Day 1, Day 2 and Day 3**. The nine values become one feature vector (`X`). The label on Day 3, `flood_within_24h`, is assigned to the next calendar day as `flood_tomorrow` (`y`). **Example:** January 1–3 → prediction for January 4. The loop advances **one day at a time**, giving overlapping three-day chunks. No Day 4 measurement enters the features."
   ]
  },
