    "id": "9U5kzEpnYmiQ"
   },
   "source": [
    "## 3. Chronological train/test split\n",
    "### Exclude 2025 and keep a 70/30 time-ordered split\n",
    "**Purpose:** Remove 2025 from the experiment, sort by `target_date`, use the **earliest 70%** of chunks for training and the **latest 30%** for testing. The output is **1,020 train chunks** and **438 test chunks**. We intentionally do **not shuffle**: a future prediction should not be trained on data from a later calendar date. Adjacent windows may share input days across the boundary; that is natural for sequential forecasting, provided future information is not used."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 13,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "ggghDNarC85h",
    "outputId": "21bd7aa6-371b-41f2-aa59-31005780d122"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "Train: (1020, 11)\n",
      "Test: (438, 11)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Remove 2025\n",
    "sw90_model = sw90_chunks[\n",
    "    sw90_chunks[\"target_date\"].dt.year <= 2024].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Sort by date\n",
    "sw90_model = sw90_model.sort_values(\"target_date\").reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 70% Train / 30% Test\n",
    "split = int(len(sw90_model) * 0.7)\n",
    "\n",
    "train = sw90_model.iloc[:split]\n",
    "test = sw90_model.iloc[split:]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Train:\", train.shape)\n",
    "print(\"Test:\", test.shape)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "3j1PWnMBYmiQ"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Check how many flood examples are in each split\n",
    "**Purpose:** Compare label counts before modeling. The training set contains **43 flood labels and 977 non-flood labels**; the test set contains **7 flood labels and 431 non-flood labels**. Only **seven** positives in the test set means one correct prediction changes Recall by **14.3 percentage points**. The evaluation will be highly sensitive to individual events."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
