   ],
   "source": [
    "print(\"Train:\")\n",
    "print(train[\"flood_tomorrow\"].value_counts())\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nTest:\")\n",
    "print(test[\"flood_tomorrow\"].value_counts())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "6VirNaaDYmiQ"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Define features (`X`) and target (`y`) for SW90\n",
    "**Purpose:** Remove `target_date` and `flood_tomorrow` from the predictor matrix, keeping only the nine historical measurements. The target vectors contain the 0/1 flood labels. Excluding the label and future target date from `X` avoids a direct form of target leakage."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 15,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "xMxpETIQDiQZ",
    "outputId": "789d8880-2e11-4c6d-d4d8-1805299a17de"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "X_train: (1020, 9)\n",
      "X_test: (438, 9)\n",
      "y_train: (1020,)\n",
      "y_test: (438,)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "X_train = train.drop(columns=[\"target_date\", \"flood_tomorrow\"])\n",
    "y_train = train[\"flood_tomorrow\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "X_test = test.drop(columns=[\"target_date\", \"flood_tomorrow\"])\n",
    "y_test = test[\"flood_tomorrow\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"X_train:\", X_train.shape)\n",
    "print(\"X_test:\", X_test.shape)\n",
    "print(\"y_train:\", y_train.shape)\n",
    "print(\"y_test:\", y_test.shape)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "ZRvynuRYYmiQ"
   },
   "source": [
    "## 4. Logistic Regression — SW90-only model\n",
    "### Scale features and train the first classifier\n",
    "**Purpose:** Use `StandardScaler` because river discharge, rainfall and soil moisture have very different numerical scales. Fit the scaler **on training data only**, then transform train and test. Fit standard `LogisticRegression` and display Accuracy. The saved Train Accuracy is **95.88%** and Test Accuracy is **98.63%**. This looks strong, but class imbalance requires more detailed metrics."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 16,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "mPXaD3M6D_Ml",
    "outputId": "858c31e9-e844-4f2e-abb8-5ac45e1462e9"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "Train Accuracy: 0.9588235294117647\n",
      "Test Accuracy: 0.9863013698630136\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\n",
    "from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n",
    "\n",
    "# Standardization\n",
    "scaler = StandardScaler()\n",
    "\n",
    "X_train_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X_train)\n",
    "X_test_scaled = scaler.transform(X_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Logistic Regression\n",
    "log_model = LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000)\n",
    "\n",
    "log_model.fit(X_train_scaled, y_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Accuracy\n",
    "print(\"Train Accuracy:\", log_model.score(X_train_scaled, y_train))\n",
    "print(\"Test Accuracy:\", log_model.score(X_test_scaled, y_test))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "gU02M4U7YmiQ"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Examine flood precision, recall and the confusion matrix\n",
    "**Purpose:** Evaluate how often the SW90 model identifies real positive labels. The test matrix is **[[430, 1], [5, 2]]**: 430 true negatives, 1 false positive, 5 missed flood days, and **2 correctly detected flood days**. The positive-class **Precision = 0.67**, **Recall = 0.29** and **F1 = 0.40**. This is more informative than Accuracy alone."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "Oh8fKdvkEJSK",
    "outputId": "5380b912-073c-453e-e5df-2047235b0181"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "[[430   1]\n",
      " [  5   2]]\n",
      "              precision    recall  f1-score   support\n",
      "\n",
      "         0.0       0.99      1.00      0.99       431\n",
      "         1.0       0.67      0.29      0.40         7\n",
      "\n",
      "    accuracy                           0.99       438\n",
      "   macro avg       0.83      0.64      0.70       438\n",
      "weighted avg       0.98      0.99      0.98       438\n",
      "\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.metrics import confusion_matrix, classification_report\n",
    "\n",
    "# Predictions\n",
    "y_pred = log_model.predict(X_test_scaled)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Confusion Matrix\n",
    "print(confusion_matrix(y_test, y_pred))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Classification Report\n",
    "print(classification_report(y_test, y_pred, zero_division=0))"
   ]
  },
