    "id": "OAwNq0tXYmiS"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Keep exactly the same train/test dates\n",
    "**Purpose:** Use the original SW90 train and test `target_date` values to select combined-station windows. This makes the comparison fair: differences should come from the **input features**, not from shifting the training or testing period. The output remains **1,020 training and 438 testing rows**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 23,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "Io7KznyjGo7s",
    "outputId": "a1d3d009-df38-408b-9e47-a8ac07b25155"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "Train: (1020, 20)\n",
      "Test: (438, 20)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Same dates as Model 1 (SW90 only)\n",
    "\n",
    "train_combined = sw90_sw17_chunks[\n",
    "    sw90_sw17_chunks[\"target_date\"].isin(train[\"target_date\"])].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "test_combined = sw90_sw17_chunks[\n",
    "    sw90_sw17_chunks[\"target_date\"].isin(test[\"target_date\"])].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Train:\", train_combined.shape)\n",
    "print(\"Test:\", test_combined.shape)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "okOEr1YZYmiS"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Confirm the label distribution stayed unchanged\n",
    "**Purpose:** A valid comparison must preserve the target labels. The same counts reappear: **43 floods in train and 7 in test**. The station combination changes the predictors, **not** the definition of a flood."
