   },
   "source": [
    "### Define the 18-feature train and test matrices\n",
    "**Purpose:** Construct `X_train_combined` and `X_test_combined` from the combined three-day measurements and assign SW90's `flood_tomorrow` as `y`. The shapes (**1,020 × 18**, **438 × 18**) confirm the additional inputs from SW17."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 25,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "RmTPANpLG0uR",
    "outputId": "0d023b88-92f6-48af-f175-2853ca92a72f"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "X_train: (1020, 18)\n",
      "X_test: (438, 18)\n",
      "y_train: (1020,)\n",
      "y_test: (438,)\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "X_train_combined = train_combined.drop(\n",
    "    columns=[\"target_date\", \"flood_tomorrow\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "X_test_combined = test_combined.drop(\n",
    "    columns=[\"target_date\", \"flood_tomorrow\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "y_train_combined = train_combined[\"flood_tomorrow\"]\n",
    "y_test_combined = test_combined[\"flood_tomorrow\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"X_train:\", X_train_combined.shape)\n",
    "print(\"X_test:\", X_test_combined.shape)\n",
    "print(\"y_train:\", y_train_combined.shape)\n",
    "print(\"y_test:\", y_test_combined.shape)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "Og7JKrieYmiT"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Train Logistic Regression with both stations\n",
    "**Purpose:** Repeat the same Logistic Regression method and train-only standardization, now using all 18 chunk features. This is a controlled feature comparison. Saved Test Accuracy is **97.95%**, a little below the SW90-only result of **98.63%**; Accuracy alone still does not tell the whole story."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 26,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "uW-O5tJ4G8AX",
    "outputId": "0e30430c-d7b1-4161-aaf3-b409d78739c7"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "Train Accuracy: 0.9568627450980393\n",
      "Test Accuracy: 0.9794520547945206\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Standardization\n",
    "scaler_combined = StandardScaler()\n",
    "\n",
    "X_train_combined_scaled = scaler_combined.fit_transform(X_train_combined)\n",
    "X_test_combined_scaled = scaler_combined.transform(X_test_combined)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Logistic Regression\n",
    "log_model_combined = LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000)\n",
    "\n",
    "log_model_combined.fit(X_train_combined_scaled, y_train_combined)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Accuracy\n",
    "print(\"Train Accuracy:\", log_model_combined.score(\n",
    "    X_train_combined_scaled, y_train_combined))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Test Accuracy:\", log_model_combined.score(\n",
    "    X_test_combined_scaled, y_test_combined))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "O5UE9jQvYmiT"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Evaluate Logistic Regression with SW90 + SW17\n",
    "**Purpose:** The test confusion matrix is **[[428, 3], [6, 1]]**. The model detects **1 of 7 positive days**, misses 6 and makes 3 false alarms. Its positive-class **Recall = 0.14** and **F1 = 0.18**. On this test period, adding all SW17 measurements **did not improve** the SW90-only Logistic Regression model."
   ]
