    "    \"prob_sw90_sw17\",\n",
    "    \"prediction_sw90\",\n",
    "    \"prediction_sw90_sw17\"]]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "C5Vb5v4vYmiU"
   },
   "source": [
    "## 6. Exploratory feature selection and validation\n",
    "### Model 3: SW90 plus only river discharge from SW17\n",
    "**Purpose:** Retain the nine SW90 features and add SW17 river discharge for each of the three days, for **12 features**. This checks whether the SW17 signal comes mainly from river discharge instead of rainfall and soil moisture. It is an **exploratory** alternative, not a replacement of our main model."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 30,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "zXwe2n1AHt4y",
    "outputId": "9d35952f-b860-435c-b10c-e42ca5499d79"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "X shape: (1020, 12)\n",
      "y shape: (1020,)\n",
      "\n",
      "Features:\n",
      "['rainfall_local_mm_sw90_day1', 'soil_moisture_local_sw90_day1', 'river_discharge_m3s_sw90_day1', 'river_discharge_m3s_sw17_day1', 'rainfall_local_mm_sw90_day2', 'soil_moisture_local_sw90_day2', 'river_discharge_m3s_sw90_day2', 'river_discharge_m3s_sw17_day2', 'rainfall_local_mm_sw90_day3', 'soil_moisture_local_sw90_day3', 'river_discharge_m3s_sw90_day3', 'river_discharge_m3s_sw17_day3']\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Model 3: SW90 + river discharge from SW17\n",
    "\n",
    "features_model3 = [\n",
    "    col for col in X_train_combined.columns\n",
    "    if \"_sw90_\" in col\n",
    "    or \"river_discharge_m3s_sw17_\" in col]\n",
    "\n",
    "X_train_model3 = train_combined[features_model3]\n",
    "y_train_model3 = train_combined[\"flood_tomorrow\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"X shape:\", X_train_model3.shape)\n",
    "print(\"y shape:\", y_train_model3.shape)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nFeatures:\")\n",
    "print(features_model3)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "uhXIe04bYmiU"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Create an internal chronological validation period\n",
    "**Purpose:** Split the original training portion into **816 earlier chunks for training** and **204 later chunks for validation** (80/20 within the original train period). The validation group has **11 flood-positive days**, and its purpose is to compare features or settings **without repeatedly choosing according to test performance**. This is distinct from the final 70/30 train/test split."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 31,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "IHYpRgtYH2wX",
    "outputId": "23d87c60-1aae-4b89-deec-67cb1e237144"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "Train: (816, 12)\n",
      "Validation: (204, 12)\n",
      "\n",
      "Train floods:\n",
      "flood_tomorrow\n",
      "0.0    784\n",
      "1.0     32\n",
      "Name: count, dtype: int64\n",
      "\n",
      "Validation floods:\n",
      "flood_tomorrow\n",
      "0.0    193\n",
      "1.0     11\n",
      "Name: count, dtype: int64\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Chronological validation split\n",
    "split_val = int(len(X_train_model3) * 0.8)\n",
    "\n",
    "X_tr = X_train_model3.iloc[:split_val]\n",
    "X_val = X_train_model3.iloc[split_val:]\n",
    "\n",
    "y_tr = y_train_model3.iloc[:split_val]\n",
    "y_val = y_train_model3.iloc[split_val:]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Train:\", X_tr.shape)\n",
    "print(\"Validation:\", X_val.shape)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nTrain floods:\")\n",
    "print(y_tr.value_counts())\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nValidation floods:\")\n",
    "print(y_val.value_counts())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "napjXmlSYmiU"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Train the 12-feature Logistic Regression on the internal split\n",
    "**Purpose:** Fit a fresh scaler and Logistic Regression only on the 816-row internal training sample; evaluate on the later 204 validation chunks. The recorded Validation Accuracy is about **94.12%**. The next cell checks whether that accuracy corresponds to actual flood detection."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 32,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "sHY2hoMvH_RC",
    "outputId": "472739f2-17b0-469a-8df4-f76f6b62b395"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "Train Accuracy: 0.9620098039215687\n",
      "Validation Accuracy: 0.9411764705882353\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Standardization\n",
    "scaler_model3 = StandardScaler()\n",
    "\n",
    "X_tr_scaled = scaler_model3.fit_transform(X_tr)\n",
    "X_val_scaled = scaler_model3.transform(X_val)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Logistic Regression\n",
    "log_model3 = LogisticRegression(max_iter=1000)\n",
    "\n",
    "log_model3.fit(X_tr_scaled, y_tr)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Accuracy\n",
    "print(\"Train Accuracy:\", log_model3.score(X_tr_scaled, y_tr))\n",
    "print(\"Validation Accuracy:\", log_model3.score(X_val_scaled, y_val))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "7p5sbkKDYmiV"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Evaluate Model 3 on validation\n",
    "**Purpose:** Its confusion matrix is **[[191, 2], [10, 1]]**, so it detected **1 of 11 flood-labeled days** and produced two false alarms. Positive-class Recall is **0.09**, F1 about **0.14**. Restricting SW17 to river discharge did not clearly improve detection on this validation period."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 33,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "EzRK8jRyIBiy",
    "outputId": "ce424b33-d57c-41b7-a3b8-2f674e8922e2"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "Confusion Matrix:\n",
      "[[191   2]\n",
      " [ 10   1]]\n",
      "\n",
      "Classification Report:\n",
      "              precision    recall  f1-score   support\n",
      "\n",
      "         0.0       0.95      0.99      0.97       193\n",
      "         1.0       0.33      0.09      0.14        11\n",
      "\n",
      "    accuracy                           0.94       204\n",
      "   macro avg       0.64      0.54      0.56       204\n",
      "weighted avg       0.92      0.94      0.92       204\n",
      "\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Predictions\n",
    "y_pred_model3 = log_model3.predict(X_val_scaled)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Confusion Matrix:\")\n",
    "print(confusion_matrix(y_val, y_pred_model3))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nClassification Report:\")\n",
    "print(classification_report(\n",
    "    y_val,\n",
    "    y_pred_model3,\n",
    "    zero_division=0))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "KoLiq_bTYmiV"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Refit SW90-only Logistic Regression on the same validation split\n",
    "**Purpose:** Train the SW90-only classifier on the **same calendar period** used for Model 3. This prevents an unfair comparison between a model measured on test and a different model measured on validation. The observed confusion matrix matches Model 3 (**one of 11 flood days detected**), although equal aggregate matrices do not prove identical daily decisions."
   ]
  },
