    "id": "shwqoHmaYmiY"
   },
   "source": [
    "## 8. Explore upstream rainfall as another feature\n",
    "### Add upstream rainfall to each three-day window\n",
    "**Purpose:** Map `rainfall_upstream_mm` from SW90 onto the three **historical** dates of every chunk. We add only one upstream-rainfall series, rather than duplicate the same information for both stations. This extends the predictors from **18 to 21** and produces **1,824 rows × 23 columns** including date and label. The target and forecast horizon stay unchanged."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 50,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "JdAFuR3sOv2a",
    "outputId": "e556a22e-a3b1-4229-aab4-b46b9b8f9c60"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "Shape: (1824, 23)\n",
      "   rainfall_upstream_mm_day1  rainfall_upstream_mm_day2  \\\n",
      "0                   0.000000                   0.000000   \n",
      "1                   0.000000                   0.000000   \n",
      "2                   0.000000                   0.000000   \n",
      "3                   0.000000                   0.533333   \n",
      "4                   0.533333                   0.644444   \n",
      "\n",
      "   rainfall_upstream_mm_day3 target_date  flood_tomorrow  \n",
      "0                   0.000000  2021-01-04             0.0  \n",
      "1                   0.000000  2021-01-05             0.0  \n",
      "2                   0.533333  2021-01-06             0.0  \n",
      "3                   0.644444  2021-01-07             0.0  \n",
      "4                   0.355556  2021-01-08             0.0  \n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Copy existing chunks\n",
    "rf_plus_chunks = sw90_sw17_chunks.copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Upstream rainfall by date\n",
    "upstream = sw90.set_index(\"date\")[\"rainfall_upstream_mm\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add upstream rainfall for each of the 3 days\n",
    "for day in [1, 2, 3]:\n",
    "\n",
    "    rf_plus_chunks[f\"rainfall_upstream_mm_day{day}\"] = (\n",
    "        rf_plus_chunks[\"target_date\"] - pd.Timedelta(days=4-day)).map(upstream)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Shape:\", rf_plus_chunks.shape)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(rf_plus_chunks[[\n",
    "    \"rainfall_upstream_mm_day1\",\n",
    "    \"rainfall_upstream_mm_day2\",\n",
    "    \"rainfall_upstream_mm_day3\",\n",
    "    \"target_date\",\n",
    "    \"flood_tomorrow\"]].head())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "94BXy9UIYmiZ"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Reuse the existing Random Forest dates and inspect missing values\n",
    "**Purpose:** Select the identical 1,020 train dates and 438 test dates used by the 18-feature forest. The saved output shows **21 predictors** and **no missing values**. This controls for sample differences while exploring whether the extra upstream data matter."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 51,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "9kIILbIXO5fO",
    "outputId": "13042f99-a6f3-41d8-8769-294fd27ba1f8"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "X_train: (1020, 21)\n",
      "X_test: (438, 21)\n",
      "\n",
      "Missing values: 0 0\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Same Train/Test dates as previous Random Forest\n",
    "\n",
    "train_rf_plus = rf_plus_chunks[\n",
    "    rf_plus_chunks[\"target_date\"].isin(train_rf[\"target_date\"])].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "test_rf_plus = rf_plus_chunks[\n",
    "    rf_plus_chunks[\"target_date\"].isin(test_rf[\"target_date\"])].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Define X and y\n",
    "X_train_rf_plus = train_rf_plus.drop(\n",
    "    columns=[\"target_date\", \"flood_tomorrow\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "X_test_rf_plus = test_rf_plus.drop(\n",
    "    columns=[\"target_date\", \"flood_tomorrow\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "y_train_rf_plus = train_rf_plus[\"flood_tomorrow\"]\n",
    "y_test_rf_plus = test_rf_plus[\"flood_tomorrow\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"X_train:\", X_train_rf_plus.shape)\n",
    "print(\"X_test:\", X_test_rf_plus.shape)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nMissing values:\", X_train_rf_plus.isnull().sum().sum(),\n",
    "      X_test_rf_plus.isnull().sum().sum())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "nNWc5mnOYmiZ"
   },
   "source": [
    "### Compare Random Forest with and without upstream rainfall\n",
    "**Purpose:** Train another `max_depth=5` Random Forest with 21 features. Both versions record **98.63% Test Accuracy, one detected flood and zero false alarms**. Adding upstream rainfall did **not** improve these classification metrics in this experiment. The next comparison checks whether individual 0/1 predictions also stayed identical."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 52,
   "metadata": {
    "colab": {
     "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
    },
    "id": "o1wbYjLBPBP7",
    "outputId": "971d1971-3fb6-45ff-b70f-7bae477c535e"
   },
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
     "text": [
      "Train Accuracy: 0.9745098039215686\n",
      "Test Accuracy: 0.9863013698630136\n",
      "\n",
      "Confusion Matrix:\n",
      "[[431   0]\n",
      " [  6   1]]\n",
      "\n",
      "Classification Report:\n",
      "              precision    recall  f1-score   support\n",
      "\n",
      "         0.0       0.99      1.00      0.99       431\n",
      "         1.0       1.00      0.14      0.25         7\n",
      "\n",
      "    accuracy                           0.99       438\n",
      "   macro avg       0.99      0.57      0.62       438\n",
      "weighted avg       0.99      0.99      0.98       438\n",
      "\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Random Forest with upstream rainfall\n",
    "rf_plus = RandomForestClassifier(\n",
    "    max_depth=5,\n",
    "    random_state=42)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Train model\n",
    "rf_plus.fit(X_train_rf_plus, y_train_rf_plus)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Accuracy\n",
    "print(\"Train Accuracy:\", rf_plus.score(X_train_rf_plus, y_train_rf_plus))\n",
    "print(\"Test Accuracy:\", rf_plus.score(X_test_rf_plus, y_test_rf_plus))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Predictions\n",
    "y_pred_rf_plus = rf_plus.predict(X_test_rf_plus)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nConfusion Matrix:\")\n",
    "print(confusion_matrix(y_test_rf_plus, y_pred_rf_plus))\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nClassification Report:\")\n",
    "print(classification_report(\n",
    "    y_test_rf_plus,\n",
    "    y_pred_rf_plus,\n",
    "    zero_division=0))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {
    "id": "BexhFtzDYmiZ"
   },
   "source": [
