   "source": [
    "## 14. Short conclusion — 48-hour flood prediction\n",
    "\n",
    "This extension tested whether **three days of environmental measurements** from SW90 and SW17 could help predict flood labels **within the following 48 hours**.\n",
    "\n",
    "On the test data, **Logistic Regression achieved the highest flood F1-score (0.32)**, compared with **0.29 for Random Forest** and **0.15 for the seasonal baseline**. The seasonal rule found more flood-labeled days, but also produced many more false alarms.\n",
    "\n",
    "**My main takeaway:** predicting rare events is difficult, and high accuracy does not necessarily mean that floods are being detected. With only **12 positive test labels**, these findings are exploratory rather than a reliable early-warning system. The 48-hour experiment adds another useful comparison to the project and shows the importance of balancing missed floods against false alarms.\n",
   ]
  }
